.TH KEEPAWAY 1
.SH NAME
keepaway \- two-team basketball keep-away
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/keepaway
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Keepaway
is a port of the TempleOS game
.IR KeepAway :
a pseudo-3D basketball keep-away between two teams of three men
on a red-bordered court, viewed at 45 degrees.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Your man is the one with the light red floor shadow, on the
light cyan team; he runs toward the mouse pointer.
Get the ball to your team: a team scores 2 points when one of its
men takes possession (a hand-off or a steal) and 6 points when he
catches a pass just as it lands.
Charging into an opposing man fast enough is a foul and gives the
other team a point.
The man holding the ball dribbles; shooting throws the ball
forward and up along his heading.
The game lasts three minutes, against the clock at the top of
the screen, and the best score difference is remembered between
games.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF Right-click
.TP
.B mouse
Run toward the pointer
.TP
.B Left-click
Shoot (pass)
.TP
.B space
Shoot (pass)
.TP
.B Right-click
Jump
.TP
.B j
Jump
.TP
.B Enter
Restart
.TP
.B Esc / q
Quit
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /icons/temple/keepaway_*.mesh
The original's GrModels-generated 3D ball and man sprites.
.TP
